  bootwright / machine trust
      Inspect and maintain exact host-key trust. It observes exactly the endpoints this context
      declares and records what they present. A Machine that proves its host key another way is
      reported and left alone; a changed key is superseded only by naming it in --replace.

  Usage
    bootwright machine trust [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run   Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --machines  Select comma-separated machine names (default: all)
      --replace   Select comma-separated replacements (default: none)
      --yes       Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright machine trust --context lab --dry-run
